    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6834" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carni</span></b> , ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Celtic people in
				Upper Italy</i>, <i>east of Aquileia</i>, <i>extending to Cärnthen</i>, now <i>Krain</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 18,
				22, § 127</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
				4040</span></i>; <i>their chief town was</i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carnūs</span></b> ,
			untis, <i><span class="en">Liv. 43, 1, 2</span></i>.— Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carnĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Alpes,</span>”
				<i>the Carnic Alps</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 25, 28, § 147</span></i>
			.</div>
